 "purpose": "Colour family + value (light/mid/dark) for every colour string in Joe's live closet_meta (142 plates, snapshot closet_meta_garments_2026-09-30.json). Used by the proposed stylist rules (COL-7..COL-13, XC-*) in 2026-09-30-stylist-review-b03aa4d.md. Proposal only; not wired into the app.",
 "how_to_use": [
  "1. Lower-case each string in garment.colors[]. If it is in `raw_aliases`, replace it with the listed canonical tokens (first token = dominant). Drop tokens that map to [].",
  "2. The DOMINANT colour of a garment = canonical token of colors[0]. Harmony rules use only dominant colours; secondary colours (index 1+) are trim/accent and never count toward accent budgets, value contrast or black/navy/brown checks.",
  "3. Look up family, value (1 = lightest .. 5 = darkest) and level (1-2 light, 3 mid, 4-5 dark) in `colors`.",
  "4. Accent role depends on the piece: see `role_by_slot`. Light blue is a NEUTRAL on shirts/tops/denim, but an ACCENT on non-denim trousers, shoes and non-denim outerwear.",
  "5. Denim pieces also get a wash level from `denim_wash` (name keywords first, then dominant colour)."
 ],
